In article <SHEM.92Jan22181948@phoenix.oulu.fi> shem@phoenix.oulu.fi writes:
>Here's a couple of questions that must be really elementary but I
>haven't succeeded in finding the answer by myself. 
>
>So: how do you sell things? If I drop things at a shop, the shopkeeper
>pays no attention, and if I throw things at them, they get angry. And

    You have to be selling things the shopkeeper also sells, i.e., you
can't sell food to a hardware shopkeeper.  Gems that aren't valuable can't
be sold even to a general store.  You just drop it while in the shop to
sell it.

>Second: it seems that it's not safe to polymorph your pet. I once
>polymorphed my cat into a trapper and it nearly digested me. Is there
>some kind of a probability in a pet turning hostile when being
>polymorphed?

    That's weird; I've never had a polymorphed pet turn hostile.
Regardless of what they turn into, they're still tame.

>Finally: what exactly does a ring of regeneration do?

    Raises your hit points (not the maximum, though) at the rate of one per
move.  You use food faster when doing this.
